{
  "_comment": [
    "US ENGLISH IS LAW — the UK->US word list, as it applies to the render worker.",
    "",
    "SOURCE OF RECORD is the app repo: wpp-prospecting-app/src/lib/usEnglish.rules.json,",
    "mirrored into the Postgres table public.us_english_rules. This is a copy, because",
    "the worker is a separate repository with its own deploy (Railway) and cannot import",
    "from the app. Change the list THERE first, then copy it here in the same change.",
    "",
    "The worker renders the Executive Opening Package — the pages a prospect physically",
    "holds. A British spelling that survives to a printed PDF cannot be recalled, which",
    "is precisely why the renderer gets its own always-on gate (scripts/us_english_gate.py)",
    "rather than trusting the app-side one.",
    "",
    "Pairs are whole words, matched case-insensitively on word boundaries, so there are no",
    "prefix false positives: 'optimistic', 'realistic', 'de minimis', 'programmer',",
    "'programming', 'analyses' (the correct US plural of 'analysis') and ReportLab's",
    "drawCentredString are all left alone."
  ],
